Title: The Permit Bottleneck Is Real — And It's Getting Worse | Rayco, Inc.
Content: The Permit Bottleneck Is Real — And It's Getting Worse | Rayco, Inc. Skip to content (469) 215-4550 Rayco, Inc. Home About Services Contact Careers Blog rayco-digs.com The Permit Bottleneck Is Real — And It's Getting Worse Published May 2026 Fiber permitting delays are no longer just a nuisance — in a BEAD world, they're a project-ending risk. With construction windows tightening and state deadlines looming, every week lost to a permit kickback is a week you can't get back. The Problem: Permits Are Becoming the Critical Path As build volumes increase, permitting has moved from a background task to the critical path of most fiber deployments. Municipal backlogs are growing. ROW agencies are understaffed. And the margin for error — in the form of incomplete or inaccurate drawing packages — is shrinking to zero. What's Driving the Delays: Inaccurate or incomplete drawing packages that trigger automatic kickbacks Lack of standardization across permit packages Multiple revision cycles eating into construction windows Coordination failures between design, permitting, and construction teams What We Do About It: Our design-to-permit workflow is built specifically to address these failure points. Every drawing package we produce is reviewed against permit requirements before submission — catching issues that would otherwise come back as kickbacks weeks later. We coordinate directly with municipalities, track submission status, and manage revision cycles on behalf of our clients. The result: fewer delays, cleaner packages, and faster approval cycles. BEAD Implications: For BEAD-funded projects, permitting delays aren't just an inconvenience — they're a compliance risk. Miss a milestone, and you're not just delayed — you're potentially out of compliance with your grant terms. This is why more operators are choosing to work with design partners who manage the full design-to-permit workflow, rather than treating permitting as an afterthought. Is your permitting workflow ready for BEAD construction volumes?</tool_response>

